A58 — retry the base Xwayland with glamor off when it exits or stalls before ready

Xwayland's glamor runs on the payload's zink over the guest Vulkan driver (see
"Two Mesas" in android/README.md). On some device/driver pairs that EGL bring-up
never completes: an Adreno 750 with a self-built Turnip died with SIGABRT right
after "Failed to make EGL context current with GL", and the system driver on
non-Adreno wedges Xwayland (which is why the app sets XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR=1
there). Either way the child never writes its -displayfd, the ready-wait (A24)
sits out its 15 s deadline, and the session ends with "Failed to initialize
wlserver" — although nothing in the session needs glamor: every Vulkan guest
presents through the WSI shim, and Xwayland with XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR=1 serves
the same X clients with software rendering. A user reproduced exactly that by
forcing LIBGL_ALWAYS_SOFTWARE=1 into the container by hand.

Two changes to the ready-wait:

- A child that dies before ready is seen at once instead of at the deadline.
  wlroots reaps it in xserver_handle_ready (the -displayfd pipe hangs up,
  "Xwayland startup failed, not setting up xwm"), unlinks its sockets and
  leaves display == -1, but emits no signal; the wait now polls that field
  (has_xwayland_exited) after each dispatch and reports Exited.

- A base server that exited or stalled with glamor on is tried once more with
  XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR=1 in the environment (wlroots spawns Xwayland with
  gamescope's environ). The old server object is destroyed first — its wlroots
  half unlinks and closes the X sockets, so the replacement binds the same
  display number, which the app addresses by path (A20). A stalled child is
  SIGKILLed before that: wlroots only closes its end of the pipes and relies on
  the server dying of EPIPE, which a child wedged in its driver never reads.
  Nothing else in gamescope holds a pointer to a base server at this point.
  The retry is not attempted when XWAYLAND_NO_GLAMOR is already set, and the
  servers created later (wlserver_make_new_xwayland_server) are not retried.

The stall snapshot from A24 is still logged before the retry, so a wedge keeps
its evidence; the log then says which attempt the session is running on.
